solutions.explanation:
The exponents differ by only \(2\), so dividing by \(2^{2012}\) turns the large powers into small numbers. Since \(2^{2014}=4\cdot2^{2012}\), the original denominator is \(3\cdot2^{2012}>0\).

Dividing numerator and denominator by the nonzero number \(2^{2012}\) gives
\[
\frac{2^{2014}+2^{2012}}{2^{2014}-2^{2012}}
=\frac{2^{2014-2012}+1}{2^{2014-2012}-1}
=\frac{4+1}{4-1}
=\frac53.
\]
The value is \(\frac53\), choice C.
